WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.727
Sometimes we do not want a final classification label at all.

00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:08.467
We want the contextual token representations produced by the Transformer.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:13.532
AutoModel loads the backbone without a task-specific classification head.

00:00:13.532 --> 00:00:19.572
After tokenization, we pass the tensors through the model and read last_hidden_state.

00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:24.377
The output shape is batch size by number of tokens by hidden dimension.

00:00:24.377 --> 00:00:29.187
In DistilBERT, the hidden dimension is typically seven hundred sixty-eight.

00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:33.592
That means every token position has its own contextual vector.

00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:39.827
These vectors already include information from the surrounding sequence after passing through the model

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:45.087
layers. Do not automatically average them and assume you have a high-quality sentence embedding.

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:50.902
General hidden states were not necessarily trained for cosine similarity between sentences.

00:00:50.902 --> 00:00:56.342
If semantic search is the goal, use a model explicitly trained for sentence embeddings,

00:00:56.342 --> 00:00:58.456
which is exactly what we do next.
